 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Одна формальность  (One Small Formality)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "arkady": "Аркадий",
  "samson": "Самсон"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Still in the mayor's office, a moment later. Last time, Samson, the bully from Arkady's childhood, came to ask for a better job, and Arkady talked him into phoning his boss and quitting on the spot. Now Samson wants to know when he starts, and Arkady has one small condition. We'll hear it in Russian first; don't worry about catching every word.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Аркаш, ну что скажешь? Когда начинать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "В любой момент.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Всё, готов!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Только есть одна маленькая формальность.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Какая формальность?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Поцелуй меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Чего?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Помнишь туалет в коммунальной квартире?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Я тебе тогда сказал: ты меня ещё поцелуешь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты что, всё помнишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А я всё помню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты шутишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Нет. Я серьёзно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нет! Никогда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Не надо, Самсон. Сейчас придёт охрана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Проводите его, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Передумаешь — приходи. Должность ждёт.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Let's go back through it. Samson has just quit his old job, so he is in a hurry to start the new one.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Аркаш, ну что скажешь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Arkasha, so what do you say?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Что скажешь?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally asks 'what will you say?', while the short name ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Аркаш",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " keeps it chummy.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Когда начинать?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'When do I start?' Literally, 'when to start?' — ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Когда",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the translation for 'when', plus the action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "начинать",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is all Russian needs here. Arkady is all smiles.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "В любой момент.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Any time you like.' Literally, 'in any moment' — ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "В любой момент.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Samson doesn't need to be asked twice.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Всё, готов!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Right, I'm ready!' the Russian word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Всё",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to 'all' or 'everything', and at the start of a line it signals 'right, that's settled!'. Then Arkady slips in one more thing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Только есть одна маленькая формальность.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'There's just one small formality.' meaning formality is an easy match with English — ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "формальность,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " softened by the describing word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "маленькая.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Samson is puzzled.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Какая формальность?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What formality?' the term for 'what' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Какая,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " ending with a matching sound for 'formality'. Arkady's answer is short.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Поцелуй меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Kiss me.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Поцелуй меня,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " comes from the action word 'to kiss'; in the show he names a much cruder humiliation, which we keep polite here. Samson can't believe his ears.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Чего?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Чего?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is a blunt, streetwise cousin of the usual word for 'what?', showing instant disbelief. So Arkady reminds him of their childhood.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Помнишь туалет в коммунальной квартире?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Do you remember the toilet in the communal flat?' the term meaning 'do you remember' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Помнишь.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " It leads straight into the phrase for 'in the communal flat' — ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "в коммунальной квартире,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " where both endings shift after the little word 'in'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Я тебе тогда сказал: ты меня ещё поцелуешь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I told you back then: you'll kiss me one day.' the translation for 'back then' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "тогда,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " and the phrase ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "ещё поцелуешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " warns 'you'll kiss me yet!'. Samson is amazed.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты что, всё помнишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'What, you remember all that?' The little phrase ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты что",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " up front expresses a stunned 'wait, what?!', followed by ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "всё помнишь?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " which translates to 'you remember everything?'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А я всё помню.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Oh, I remember everything.' Opening with the little word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " in ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "А я всё помню",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " gives a quiet, icy contrast — 'oh, I remember it all'. Samson hopes it's a joke.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Ты шутишь?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you joking?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Шутишь?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'are you kidding me?', built from the expression for 'a joke'. Arkady keeps a straight face.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Нет. Я серьёзно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No. I'm serious.' Russian skips 'am' and uses ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "серьёзно:",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally 'I seriously'. Samson explodes.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Нет! Никогда!",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'No! Never!' the expression meaning 'never!' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Никогда!",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " It echoes 'no!' as Samson lunges forward, while Arkady doesn't even get up.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Не надо, Самсон. Сейчас придёт охрана.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't, Samson. Security will be here any second.' The phrase ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Не надо",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " calmly warns 'don't do that', and which translates to 'security guards' is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "охрана.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " Right on cue, they step in.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Проводите его, пожалуйста.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Please see him out.' Addressing the guards politely, Arkady adds a respectful ending to ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Проводите,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " which translates to 'escort him out'. As Samson leaves, one last line lands.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Передумаешь — приходи.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'If you change your mind, come back.' Russian needs no 'if' here: ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Передумаешь",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to 'you'll rethink it', followed by ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "приходи,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " which literally means 'come on over' — that says it all.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Должность ждёт.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The job is waiting.' the term for an official post or managerial position is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "Должность,",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " rather than the ordinary word for work. Let's listen to the whole scene once more.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Аркаш, ну что скажешь? Когда начинать?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "arkady",
   "t": "В любой момент.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "samson",
   "t": "Всё, готов!",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
